Z||000000||RaeQwan||01-03-2001||02:21 AM||||ohhhh this makes me unhappy. I start going down the road, I feel my car isn't getting up to speed quick enough(me not pushing gas hard enough) so I floor it, when I do.. its cool for about 10mph.. from bout 35-40 to 45-50.. then it hits 50mph and my rear end decides to dance.. wiggling from side to side. Someone help!!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwanegg.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||JohnnyK||01-03-2001||02:50 AM||||Well, WORST CASE scenario, you broke your cradle like I did.. Same thing happened to me. Snapped right where the rear a-arm connects to the frame. To check it, lift the rear of the car into the air and grab the tires and wiggle em.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RaeQwan||01-03-2001||06:04 AM||||Could this have happened on a 88?||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||01-03-2001||07:02 AM||||i was experiencing the same wiggle, when, after reinstallling my rear sway bar (a few months back).  after experiencing this, i decided to rebuild my suspension.<P>guess what?  the wiggle was still there.  last night, i removed the rear sway bar to see if that helps. :fingers crossed:<P>as for your car... let me ask a few questions:<BR>1) do you have a rear sway bar?<BR>2)how old are your tires (older tires can contribute to this)?<BR>3)have you done any work to it that requires dropping the cradle?<P>hope i can help some!<P>hoop||||reg||2
Z||000004||Phil||01-03-2001||07:14 AM||||Never overlook the easy things. Check tire pressure, even a 5 lb differential will make it act crazy.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gold-86SE||01-03-2001||09:35 AM||||<BR>I know that the rest of the fellas are talking about suspension, but can you tell what the source is?<P>If the source is a engine surge/hesitation maybe you need to examine those areas.  My 84 about 3 days ago gave me a nice little bump and grind when under heavy acceleration.  My problem - bad plug wires.  I spent time chasing the TPS, the idle air-control valve, distributor cap and rotor, but it was the wires.<P>Just relaying my experience, maybe it will help.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000006||RaeQwan||01-03-2001||01:59 PM||||No swaybar, Tires are 1 yearold, got em last Dec/Jan. As far as I know they are at correct tire pressure. I swapped engines in it last year, could I have done something then? <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwanegg.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||01-03-2001||03:58 PM||||the reason for my questions are that our problems seem similar... so if we can figure out one, we an figure out both!<P>1) what is the condition of the motor/tranny mounts?  i know my motor mounts are worn, and the rear tranny mount is bad, also.  i replaced the front one last year.<P>2) did you replace the half shafts, or seals in the tranny?  i have pondered the idea of the shafts "wondering" a bit.<P>3) check the toe in on the rear.  too much, or too little could also affect this.<P>||||reg||1
